Subject: [PATCH 1/1] radv/ps5: the host model flushes with CLFLUSH, which every
 x86-64 CPU has

Grapnel's shaders' preparation runs this driver on the player's PC, on the PS5
winsys's host model. radv_ps5_cpu_flush wrote CLFLUSHOPT lines whatever the
CPU, and the model zeroes and flushes every GTT buffer it makes
(radv_ps5_bo.c): on Intel's CPUs before Skylake and AMD's before Zen, which
have no CLFLUSHOPT, the preparation stopped at its first buffer with an illegal
instruction (exit 0xC000001D on an i5-4670K, 25/11/2026).

Off the console the lines go out with CLFLUSH, between the same two MFENCEs.
The console's driver compiles exactly as before (__PROSPERO__); nothing that
the shader cache keys or holds changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.c b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.c
index b8335d7ae69..fc76ed36c55 100644
--- a/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.c
+++ b/src/amd/vulkan/winsys/ps5/radv_ps5_platform.c
@@ -186,7 +186,17 @@ radv_ps5_cpu_flush(const void *address, size_t bytes)
     * GPU wrote). A submission's words took one serialising CLFLUSH a line. */
    __builtin_ia32_mfence();
    for (; at < end; at += line)
+#if defined(__PROSPERO__)
       __asm__ volatile("clflushopt %0" : "+m"(*(volatile char *)at));
+#else
+      /* (Grapnel's shaders' preparation on a PC, the host model: CLFLUSH,
+       * which every x86-64 CPU has. CLFLUSHOPT is not on Intel's before
+       * Skylake nor AMD's before Zen, and the preparation stopped there at its
+       * first zeroed buffer (0xC000001D on an i5-4670K, 25/11/2026). Nothing
+       * runs on a GPU here: what the console gains from CLFLUSHOPT does not
+       * matter, the closing MFENCE orders the lines as before) */
+      __asm__ volatile("clflush %0" : "+m"(*(volatile char *)at));
+#endif
    __builtin_ia32_mfence();
 }
 
